.nh
.TH "RAIL0" "1" "Aug 2026" "rail0 CLI" ""

.SH NAME
rail0-payouts-destinations-add - Register a payout destination (asks you to confirm the details)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrail0 payouts destinations add [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Register a deposit address as a payout destination of the session's wallet.

.PP
Before running it, open the venue's deposit page with the NETWORK set to --chain
and the asset set to --token, and copy the address and the minimum deposit from
there.

.PP
The minimum is required, and stated explicitly: --min-amount  (the
figure; 0 is an ordinary figure), or --no-minimum when the venue has none — never
both. On a terminal, leaving both out prompts for it (an empty answer is not
accepted: type "none" if the venue has none); without a terminal or with --agent
it is a usage error, before any request.

.PP
The command shows what it will register and the details statement, and you must
accept it: a y/N prompt (default no) on a terminal, or --confirm-details when
there is no terminal or with --agent. Without it nothing is sent. --yes does not
accept it for you.

.PP
--token is a symbol (USDC) resolved on --chain, or the token's 0x address;
--chain and --token fall back to the configured defaults ('rail0 config').
--min-amount and --reserve are decimals in token units (10.00), never negative,
converted with the token's decimals. --wallet defaults to the wallet you are
signed in with, and must be it.

.PP
The destination is born "unverified". Next: send the proof with
\&'rail0 payouts send --destination  --proof', and once the venue shows it
credited, 'rail0 payouts destinations confirm \&'.

.PP
Refused (422): the zero address, the wallet itself, a contract the gateway knows on
that chain, no minimum stated (minimum_required), both a figure and --no-minimum
(minimum_conflict), or no confirmation; 409 when the wallet already has this
address for this token and chain.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-A\fP, \fB--address\fP=""
	The venue's deposit address (0x…, or @alias)

.PP
\fB-c\fP, \fB--chain\fP=
	Chain the deposit address was issued for (default: 'rail0 config' chain): a slug (arc, base, …) or a chain id; the environment's gateway decides testnet vs mainnet

.PP
\fB--confirm-details\fP[=false]
	Accept the details statement without a prompt (needed without a TTY or with --agent); --yes does NOT imply it

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for add

.PP
\fB--kind\fP=""
	Informational: exchange, circle_mint, self_custody, provider (default exchange)

.PP
\fB-l\fP, \fB--label\fP=""
	Human-readable label

.PP
\fB--min-amount\fP=""
	The venue's minimum deposit, decimal in token units (e.g. 10.00) — required, or --no-minimum

.PP
\fB--no-minimum\fP[=false]
	The venue has no minimum deposit (no_minimum: true); excludes --min-amount

.PP
\fB--reserve\fP=""
	Refund reserve left in the wallet on '--amount all', decimal in token units

.PP
\fB-t\fP, \fB--token\fP=""
	Token symbol (USDC) or 0x address on that chain (default: 'rail0 config' token)

.PP
\fB--wallet\fP=""
	Wallet that will send to it, id or address (default: the signed-in wallet)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--agent\fP[=false]
	Agent mode: one JSON envelope on stdout, JSON events on stderr, no prompts (env: RAIL0_AGENT=1)

.PP
\fB--base-url\fP=""
	RAIL0 gateway base URL (env: RAIL0_BASE_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Print HTTP request/response details to stderr

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Force plain (uncolored) JSON output (useful in scripts)

.PP
\fB--pretty\fP[=false]
	Use the key-value/table view instead of JSON (terminal only)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Print only the result's id/hash, one per line (useful in scripts)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  rail0 payouts destinations add -c arc -t USDC -A 0xVenueDeposit… \\
    -l "Exchange USDC (Arc)" --min-amount 10

  # non-interactive: state the minimum and accept the statement explicitly
  rail0 payouts destinations add -c arc -t USDC -A 0xVenueDeposit… --no-minimum --confirm-details
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBrail0-payouts-destinations(1)\fP
